  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dynetics has FY2026 to date federal contract obligations totaling $1B across 36 awards, with an average award size of $28.5M and obligations up 61.5% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1B to Dynetics in the current year to date. Other federal buyers include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $8.4M and the General Services Administration with $2.2M. Fiscal-year obligations show a multiyear pattern: FY21 $420M, FY22 $178M, FY23 $117M, FY24 $137M, FY25 $636M and FY26 $1B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market for Dynetics, receiving $870M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $133M. Additional recorded markets include Engineering Services $10.5M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) $9.1M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing $4.4M. The dataset also shows Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing with $0 in obligations for the period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main federal buyers for Dynetics?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the main federal buyer for Dynetics, obligating $1B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $8.4M, and the General Services Administration follows with $2.2M. These three agencies account for the bulk of recorded obligations in the current year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and NAICS codes drive Dynetics obligations?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing drives the largest share of Dynetics obligations with $870M in FY2026 to date. Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $133M, while Engineering Services accounts for $10.5M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $9.1M. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $4.4M."
      }
